export anchor ChessNotationStyle:
    number: 101
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Chess notation
    idea: The dashboard kept like a tournament scoresheet, with board files for navigation, the totals on a checkered rank, projects in a standings table with chess pieces and annotation marks, and activity written as numbered moves.
    base: light
    palette:
        scoresheet: #fbfaf7, the page, tables and fields
        ink: #161616, text, rules, week two squares and the primary button
        graphite: #3b3b3b, meta, legends and axis labels
        walnut: #6b4a2b, dark board squares, week one squares and file letters
        lightSquare: #f1e9da, light board squares and header cells
        darkSquare: #e2d4bb, empty dark squares on the chart and the focus halo
        green: #24603e, On track
        amber: #8a5200, At risk
        red: #a02020, Behind and overdue
    type:
        Headings use Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Segoe UI,
        sans-serif. Body uses Georgia, serif. Notation and numbers use
        ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is 30
        to 44px Futura at 500, summary numbers 52px mono bold, block heads
        18px Futura caps tracked 0.14em, project names 16px Georgia, notation
        14px mono and legends 13px Georgia.
    layout:
        The header has a king glyph and the caps brand at left and a mono
        search field, the bell and a black New project button at right. A
        ruled scoresheet table below gives Player Mara Okafor and the date.
        The nav is a full width row of ruled cells, each with a walnut file
        letter a to f, the current cell filled black. The greeting sits left
        with Check. 4 tasks are overdue at right. The four totals are one
        checkered rank of alternating light and walnut squares in a 2px ink
        frame. Standings is a ruled table with number, a chess piece for the
        team, project and team, tasks as 18/25, a rank of eight squares
        filled for progress with the percent, due date and status, with
        striped rows. Below, Fourteen ranks, two checkered boards of seven
        files each filled one square per task, sits beside Moves, a numbered
        list with a short walnut mono code, the plain sentence and the time.
        On phones the table becomes stacked rows and the nav wraps into
        three cells across.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 8 to 10px table cell padding and 40px between blocks.
    density: Dense and orderly, like a scoresheet. Tables carry most of the content.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: 1px ink rules for tables and the nav, 2px ink rules under block heads and around the totals rank.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Unicode chess pieces for teams, a bishop for Design, a rook for
        Engineering, a knight for Research and a queen for Marketing, and a
        king for the brand. Annotation marks are drawn in SVG, an
        exclamation in a circle for On track, a query and exclamation in a
        diamond for At risk, and a double query in a solid square for Behind
        and overdue, each with the word.
    focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px dark square halo.
    tone: Terse tournament shorthand with a plain sentence beside it, such as Check, Standings, Fourteen ranks and Moves.
